// Deflate and inflate, bound to miniz.
//
// There is no `dependencies` block because miniz depends on nothing a package manager could fetch --
// it is two files, both carried here, and what they include from the C library is `<assert.h>`,
// `<stdlib.h>` and `<string.h>`. It is not a library anybody has installed.
//
// This is the block a *consumer* writes to reach this package:
//
//     dependencies {
//       miniz { git = "github.com/sysl-lang/miniz", version = "0.3.1" }
//     }
//
// The coordinate is identity rather than a URL, so it carries no `https://`, and the version is the
// tag `v0.3.1` on this repository.

package {
  name    = "miniz"
  version = "0.3.1"

  // **The floor is the compiler `Decoder` was written and tested against.** It was 0.0.81 before
  // that, for `sysl.slices.align_up`, and 0.0.65 before that, for the `defines` block below. It is a
  // key so that an older compiler is refused rather than failing on a name it has never heard of.
  sysl = "0.1.3"
}

// **There is deliberately no `requires` block, though `requires {}` would be exact.**
//
// A capability clause is a claim about what a library *does*, and what miniz does here is arithmetic
// on buffers it was handed. It opens no file, reads no clock, and calls no allocator -- not because
// the calls are unused but because `MINIZ_NO_MALLOC` removes them, along with `MINIZ_NO_STDIO`,
// `MINIZ_NO_TIME` and `MINIZ_NO_ARCHIVE_APIS` taking the `.zip` reader and every heap-returning
// helper with them. Even the compressor's 167,800-byte working state is storage the caller places.
//
// **Whether the headers exist on a bare target is the C toolchain's business, and there they do
// not.** `miniz.h` includes `<assert.h>`, `<stdlib.h>` and `<string.h>` unconditionally; clang gives
// a freestanding target none of the three, so `--target thumb-freestanding` fails on the include.
// This was run rather than reasoned about. A target with a libc is fine, which includes the Pico
// SDK's newlib, Zephyr and a FreeRTOS application -- see the README's "What is still hosted about
// it".
//
// **The build options are the `defines` block below**, which needs sysl 0.0.65 or later. Until
// 0.1.1 they lived in an `options.h` that every translation unit included, because nothing supplied
// a `-D` to a package's own C; the manifest now does, and the wrapper is gone with it. The `sysl`
// key above states a later floor than 0.0.65 for a different reason, given there.
//
// The raw layer's tests assert the state sizes those options produce, so a setting that stopped
// applying fails a test rather than costing 151,552 bytes of somebody's SRAM.
//
// **What is NOT here is a `@link` directive**, and the absence is the point of vendoring: the
// implementation is compiled from the `.c` carried in this package, so there is no external library
// for the linker to be given.

// What miniz's own C is compiled with.
//
// **Every one of these either deletes symbols or changes the size of a state struct this package
// exports as a constant**, so the two C files and the `c const` block beside them have to agree.
// Two things arrange that rather than one. The braced key gives both files **one** copy of the list,
// so there is nothing to drift; and a `c const` block inherits the macros of the carried C in its
// own directory, so the probe agrees with the objects without being named at all.
//
// `MINIZ_NO_MALLOC` is the one that makes this package what it is -- without it miniz's zlib-style
// API allocates its own state and the caller-owned arrangement becomes one of two ways to do the
// same thing. `MINIZ_NO_STDIO` drops the `FILE *` API, `MINIZ_NO_ARCHIVE_APIS` the `.zip` reader and
// writer, and `MINIZ_NO_TIME` the archive timestamps and the clock they need.
//
// `TDEFL_LESS_MEMORY` takes the compressor's state from 319,352 bytes to 167,800, for slightly worse
// ratios and more frequent raw blocks. **It is also the one option a `-D` cannot reach**: upstream's
// header defines it unguarded, so the vendored copy carries an `#ifndef` around that line and it is
// the only difference from the release tarball.
defines {
  "sh/sysl/miniz/c/{miniz,shim}.c" {
    MINIZ_NO_MALLOC       = true
    MINIZ_NO_STDIO        = true
    MINIZ_NO_ARCHIVE_APIS = true
    MINIZ_NO_TIME         = true
    TDEFL_LESS_MEMORY     = 1
  }
}
